<title>GERMANY: Siemens says it too will cut sick pay.</title>
<headline>Siemens says it too will cut sick pay.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>German electronics and engineering giant Siemens AG said it too would cut sick pay shortly, joining the ranks of German employers planning to implement quickly a recent change in labour laws.</p>
<p>Siemens said it would cut sick pay to 80 percent of normal wages as soon as the new rules take effect.</p>
<p>Sick pay at Siemens, which employs 210,000 workers in Germany, totaled 380 million marks ($252.3 million) last year.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150 ($ = 1.506 German Marks)</p>
